// The four elemental pillars of Map 11: look() for shape 865.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS IS PINNED TO 865 AND CANNOT MOVE. The engine picks the
// usecode class for an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER:
//
//     uint32 class_id = _shape;          // item.cpp:1516
//
// so shape 865's look() lands in class 865 and nowhere else, the way the
// gods' anim() lands in 860 (GODANIM.UNK) and the Message Scroll's read in
// 864 (MSGSCRL.UNK). `lv_manifest.json` pins TYPEELEMENTALCOLUMN to 865
// for that reason. Decided by Douglas on 2026-09-24 against
// docs/art-track.md contract 5, open decision 1: the pillars speak.
//
// THIS CLASS IS DEAD UNTIL THE ART LANDS. Shape 865 is reserved and not
// yet injected (the pillars are still shape 721, the engine's CHIMNEY, and
// a click on one still says "chimney"). Nothing on any map dispatches
// here today. When lv_art_props.py injects 865 and build_map_11.py places
// it, this look() answers with no further change.
//
// THE NAME IS THE DESIGN DOC'S, AND IT IS SAFE. COLPUZZL.UNK:139 filters
// `type = TypeElementalColumn`, and that identifier must keep resolving to
// the shape ON THE MAP (721 today, 865 after the re-point). It does: the
// codegen resolves a Type identifier through TYPE_SHAPES before it ever
// consults the class table (u8c_codegen.py, the foreach filter at :1686
// and the value path at :2267 both call get_type_shape first; the class
// lookup is the fallback at :2354). So declaring this typeclass changes
// nothing COLPUZZL compiles. The TYPE_SHAPES re-point 721 -> 865 stays a
// separate, deliberate edit that lands with the art.
//
// THE BARKS follow the ELEMENT, and the element follows the MAP's frame
// order (build_map_11.py, decision 2026-07-04): 0 Earth, 1 Air, 2 Fire,
// 3 Water. The dialogue design doc's bark table listed the older order for
// two months and was remapped 2026-09-22; the text is its text, the
// mapping is the map's. The doc's "shattered remains of a column" has no
// home here, because TypeReceptacle::use() destroys the pillar outright.

uses "item";

typeclass TypeElementalColumn inherits Item
{
	process look();
}

process TypeElementalColumn::look()
{
	f:Number = 0;

	f = getFrame();

	if f = 0
	{
		bark("column of solid stone");
		return;
	}
	if f = 1
	{
		bark("column of swirling wind");
		return;
	}
	if f = 2
	{
		bark("column of roaring flame");
		return;
	}
	if f = 3
	{
		bark("column of shimmering water");
		return;
	}

	// A frame the map never places. Naming the thing beats silence.
	bark("column");
}
